# Git commit messages

Personal project — no ticket prefix.

## Subject format

```text
(feat) Short summary of the change
```

- **Type** in parentheses (lowercase): `feat`, `fix`, `debug`, `docs`, `perf`, `refactor`, `chore`.
- **Summary**: concise phrase after the type. Focus on why, not a file dump.

## Small change

One subject line only, no body:

```text
(fix) Route movie list through @AppApi
```

## Large change

Same subject, then a blank line and a numbered list of concrete points:

```text
(feat) Split the backend into feature modules

1. Pull Spring Boot into app and add shared/core
2. Add one Maven module per feature
3. Document layout and Cursor layer rules
```

## When committing

- Subject-only for small diffs (one concern / few files).
- Numbered body when the commit spans multiple concerns or many files.
- Pass the message via HEREDOC as required by the commit workflow.
- Do not add Co-authored-by unless the user asks.
- Do not invent ticket IDs (`ZC-123`, etc.).
